                  "external/cert/obligation/rule"
                ],
                "description": "Using placement new with pointers without sufficient storage capacity creates\n              objects which can overflow the bounds of the allocated memory leading to undefined\n              behaviour.",
                "id": "cpp/cert/placement-new-insufficient-storage-cert",
                "kind": "path-problem",
                "name": "MEM54-CPP: Placement new shall be used only with pointers to sufficient storage capacity",
