                ],
                "description": "Deallocation functions should only be called on nullptr or a pointer returned by the\n              corresponding allocation function, that hasn't already been deallocated.",
                "id": "cpp/cert/properly-deallocate-dynamically-allocated-resources",
                "kind": "problem",
                "name": "MEM51-CPP: Properly deallocate dynamically allocated resources",
                "precision": "medium",
